{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791136904,"nonce":"CXdr80rDrwbLNs1mT7361qwu75M=","title":"the desktop test fails 11 checks on macOS","message":"`XWINDOW_DESKTOP=1 cargo test -p xwindow-check --test desktop` on macOS (AppKit) gives 7 passed, 2 skipped, 11 failed. CI runs it only on X11, Wayland and Windows, so this is unwatched.\n\nTwo causes:\n\n1. No input driver. keyboard, pointer, wheel, input routing and raw device events fail with \"no synthetic input on macOS\". CGEventPost needs the Accessibility permission for the test binary; a driver could post through it when it is granted and skip otherwise.\n\n2. Events from synchronous AppKit calls are lost. setSize gives no Resized, focus gives no Focused(true), setPosition gives no Moved, cursor position gives no CursorMoved, fullscreen gives no Resized, and closing one window fails the same way. AppKit calls the window delegate inside setContentSize/makeKeyWindow/setFrameOrigin, between pumps; winit then has no event handler set and drops the event, logging \"tried to run event handler, but no handler was set\". Wayland had the same gap for setSize, fixed by queueing Resized from request_inner_size's return. The macOS equivalent is to queue the event from the call's own result where it has one (size, position), or to compare state after the next pump.\n\nFailures are identical with and without the change for 1c8ea53.","files":null}]}